{"page_content": "Derivation of the removal rate constants\n\nThe total rate constant for removal is made up of several parts:\n\ne\u00ab biodegradation rate constant;\n\ne volatilisation of substance from soil;\n\ne leaching to deeper soil layers.\n\nOther removal processes may be important in some cases (e.g. uptake by plants). If rate constants are known for these processes, they may be added to the total removal. The overall removal rate constant is given by:\n\nk=Kyog +k leach + kbio. 1\n\nEquation R.16-49\n\nExplanation of symbols", "metadata": {"doc_id": "579cfc27-cffd-46ca-8002-c7a7dabcf41a", "content_type": "CompositeElement", "filename": "IR_CSR_R16_V4_FINAL.pdf"}}